==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|nat'l||abbreviation}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|frm|national}}, corresponding to {{suffix|en|nation|al}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|en|/ˈnaʃ.ə.nəl/|[ˈnaʃ.ə.nɫ̩]|;|/ˈnaʃ.n̩əl/|[ˈnaʃ.n̩ɫ̩]|a=UK}}
*{{IPA|en|/ˈnæʃ.ə.nəl/|[ˈnæʃ.ə.nɫ̩]|;|/ˈnæʃ.n̩əl/|[ˈnæʃ.n̩ɫ̩]|a=US}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-national.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|æʃənəl|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Pertaining to a [[nation]] or [[country]], especially as a whole; affecting, shared by, or existing throughout all of a nation; the [[state]]. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#: {{usex|en|a '''national''' assembly · on the front page of every '''national''' newspaper}}
#: {{usex|en|Import tariffs were raised for the '''national''' interest.}}
# Belonging to or characteristic of a specific [[nation]] or country, as opposed to others. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#: {{usex|en|this is their '''national''' dish · our '''national''' tendency to laugh at the French}}
# {{lb|en|now|rare}} [[nationalistic|Nationalistic]]; [[patriotic]]. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1791|author=w:James Boswell|title=Life of Johnson|page=599|publisher=Oxford|year_published=2008
|passage=‘Come, come, don't deny it: they are really '''national'''. Why, now, the Adams are as liberal-minded men as any in the world: but, I don't know how it is, all their workmen are Scotch.’}}

====Usage notes====
See ''[[nation]]'' for notes regarding the usage of ''national'' to refer to the UK and its member states.

