==German==

===Etymology===
{{etymon|de|:bor|la-new:nātionālis|tree=1}}
{{bor+|de|la-new|nātionālis}} and influence of {{der|de|fr|national}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˌnatsi̯oˈnaːl/|[ˌna.tsjoˈnaːl]|/ˈnatsi̯oˌnaːl/|[ˈna.tsjoˌnaːl]}}
* {{audio|de|De-national.oga}}
* {{rhymes|de|aːl|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{de-adj|comp}}

# [[#English|national]] {{gloss|being part of a nation's identity or character}}
#: {{uxi|de|eine '''nationale''' Tradition|a '''national''' tradition}}
#: {{uxi|de|die '''nationale''' Sprache (≈ ''die'' {{m|de|Nationalsprache}})|the '''national''' language}}
#: {{uxi|de|'''nationale''' Eigenarten|'''national''' characteristics}}
# [[#English|national]] {{gloss|of importance for the nation as a whole}}
#: {{uxi|de|'''nationale''' Belange|national interests}}
#: {{uxi|de|eine '''nationale''' Katastrophe|a '''national''' catastrophe}}
#: {{uxi|de|der '''nationale''' Dialog|the '''national''' dialogue}}
# [[nationwide]], [[#English|national]] {{gloss|covering a country, as opposed to regional and international levels; see usage note below}}
#: {{uxi|de|'''nationale''' Parlamente (≈ {{m|de|Nationalparlament|Nationalparlamente}})|'''national''' parliaments}}
#: {{uxi|de|auf '''nationaler''' Ebene|on the '''national''' level}}
#: {{uxi|de|die '''nationale''' Gesetzgebung|'''national''' legislation}}
# (moderately) [[nationalist]]
#: {{uxi|de|das '''nationale''' Lager|the '''nationalist''' camp}}
#: {{uxi|de|Sozialismus '''nationaler''' Prägung|socialism with a '''nationalist''' imprint}}

====Usage notes====
* The comparative forms are infrequent.
* German '''''national''''' in the sense of “nationwide” occurs chiefly in a political context, as shown in the examples above. Its use in other contexts is often modeled on English usage: {{m|de||ein nationaler Gesangswettbewerb|a national singing competition}}. The more idiomatic German word is {{m|de|landesweit}} or, in the cases of Germany and Austria specifically, {{m|de|bundesweit}}: {{m|de||ein landesweiter/bundesweiter Gesangswettbewerb}}.

